<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

<Callout kind="warn">
Three problems were merged into one ticket because
[decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line. "Wrong day on the
invite" and "Date is wrong" describe three different bugs that all produce the same sentence.
</Callout>

## The note above the table doesn't say

Read the note under the `parser` row again: **5 reports read as a one-day move; filed under
`parser` by tenant.** That is the desk's own code, from this export, saying these 5 reports
don't actually fit the cause they're filed under. A day/month swap can never move a date by
exactly one day — 07/04 ↔ 04/07 is 88 days, not 1 — so whatever is wrong with these 5, it is not
the parser bug, and it is not the hint bug either (none of them came in on the `form` channel).
Checked against the full text of all 412 reports, not against the desk's list, the same 5 are
the only ones this is true for:

- `R-41202` (kettle.books, email): "Invite says Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May."
- `R-41209` (alder.physio, app): "Every booking in June is one day off. Only June."
- `R-41236` (nine.lanterns, app): "The invite arrived before I made the booking."
- `R-41344` (pale.harbour, email): "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday.
  Same meeting. We held it twice."
- `R-41620` (lantern.row, email): "Tuesday 6 October showed as Monday."

They're still inside the 379 the table shows for `parser` — the desk's own count, as exported,
is unchanged above. They're also their own problem.

## Where each one went

- **parser** (379, the desk's own count) — filed as
  [kcprnoj/support-kb-4471#1](https://github.com/kcprnoj/support-kb-4471/issues/1). The desk's
  engineering update on #4471 (closed 5 Oct) confirms it: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu
  locales`. **Closed, fixed.**
- **hint** (33, the desk's own count) — filed as
  [kcprnoj/support-kb-4471#2](https://github.com/kcprnoj/support-kb-4471/issues/2). The same
  update marks it **won't fix: booking-v3 form retired** — the tenants that hit this no longer
  run that form, so it can't recur. **Closed, won't fix.**
- **one-day move** (5, named by the desk's own `oneDayMove` note, a subset of the 379 above) —
  filed as [kcprnoj/support-kb-4471#3](https://github.com/kcprnoj/support-kb-4471/issues/3). The
  engineering update doesn't mention it at all — it was never part of either known cause.
  **Still open.**

## Lessons

- Dedupe by subject merges by what a report *sounds like*, not by what caused it.
- A note that says "these read differently" and files them anyway is a problem waiting for a
  ticket, not a resolved footnote — the data to find it was already in the export.

